Description: interactive guitar fretboard for exploring harmony and dissonance
 Harmonic Explorer is an interactive tool for understanding why notes
 sound consonant or dissonant together, seen through the lens of a
 guitar fretboard.
 .
 It features a clickable fretboard with capo and key selection, additive
 synthesis with selectable waveforms and an ADSR envelope editor, live
 waveform and spectrum visualization, a live Plomp-Levelt dissonance
 curve for the selected notes, a chord builder with consonance analysis
 of every interval, and melody playback in the selected key.
 .
 The application is a self-contained HTML document rendered in a
 dedicated WebKitGTK window. It runs fully offline and makes no network
 connections.
